# Tracer: list-set denotation is proof-free while pairwise WD stays local.
#
# Before (Litex verified, but Lean theorem types mentioned local WD names):
# forall a, b set:
#     a != b
#     =>:
#         {a, b} = {a, b}
# Former behavior: `Litex.listSet [a, b] (by ... exact wd_0_N)` put a proof
# created after `intro` into the theorem type.
#
# Now (verified): `Litex.listSet [a, b]` is the object term, while the exact
# pairwise `WellDefinedFactId` is replayed as a local `have wd_0_N`.
# Boundary: missing, duplicated, reversed, or retargeted pair roles fail closed.
# Evidence: `LITEX_LEAN_PROJECT=lean LITEX_LAKE=lake cargo test --release
# proof_carrying_list_set_compiles_with_mathlib -- --ignored --nocapture`.

forall a, b set:
    a != b
    =>:
        {a, b} = {a, b}

forall a, b, c set:
    a != b
    a != c
    b != c
    =>:
        {a, b, c} = {a, b, c}
